---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import NewsletterForm from '../components/NewsletterForm.astro';
---

<Base
	title="How We Work | Superdots"
	description="How Superdots creates content — our AI-assisted editorial process, the team behind the articles, and what human oversight looks like."
>
	<Fragment slot="head">
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
			"@context": "https://schema.org",
			"@type": "WebPage",
			"name": "How We Work",
			"description": "How Superdots creates content — our AI-assisted editorial process, the team behind the articles, and what human oversight looks like.",
			"url": "https://superdots.sh/how-we-work/",
			"isPartOf": {
				"@type": "WebSite",
				"name": "Superdots",
				"url": "https://superdots.sh"
			},
			"about": {
				"@type": "Organization",
				"name": "Superdots",
				"url": "https://superdots.sh",
				"founder": {
					"@type": "Person",
					"name": "Luca Bartoccini",
					"jobTitle": "Founder",
					"url": "https://superdots.sh/about/luca/"
				}
			}
		})} />
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
			"@context": "https://schema.org",
			"@type": "BreadcrumbList",
			"itemListElement": [
				{ "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://superdots.sh" },
				{ "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "About", "item": "https://superdots.sh/about/" },
				{ "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "How We Work" }
			]
		})} />
	</Fragment>
	<PageHeader
		title="How we work"
		kicker="Transparency"
		subtitle="AI helps us write. Humans make sure it's worth reading. Here's exactly how our editorial process works."
		breadcrumbs={[
			{ label: 'Home', href: '/' },
			{ label: 'About', href: '/about/' },
			{ label: 'How We Work', href: '/how-we-work/' },
		]}
	/>

	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			Superdots is built by a small team of AI agents coordinated by a human editor.
			We use AI throughout our editorial process — and we think you should know exactly how.
		</p>
		<p>
			This page explains what AI does in our workflow, where humans step in, and why
			we believe this approach produces better content than either could alone.
		</p>

		<h2>The editorial pipeline</h2>
		<p>Every article on Superdots goes through a structured pipeline before it reaches you.</p>

		<div class="pipeline">
			<div class="pipeline-step">
				<div class="step-number">1</div>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Research &amp; keyword analysis</h3>
					<p>We start with data. Our SEO team identifies topics where professionals are actively searching for AI guidance — real questions from real people, not manufactured content gaps.</p>
					<span class="step-who">AI-driven, human-reviewed</span>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="pipeline-step">
				<div class="step-number">2</div>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Writing &amp; drafting</h3>
					<p>AI agents draft articles following our editorial guidelines: practical advice, clear structure, no fluff. Each article targets a specific department and use case so the guidance is relevant, not generic.</p>
					<span class="step-who">AI-drafted</span>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="pipeline-step">
				<div class="step-number">3</div>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Editorial review</h3>
					<p>A content manager reviews every draft for accuracy, clarity, and usefulness. Does this actually help someone do their job? Is the advice actionable today? If not, it goes back for revision.</p>
					<span class="step-who">AI + human review</span>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="pipeline-step">
				<div class="step-number">4</div>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Legal &amp; compliance check</h3>
					<p>Articles are checked for legal accuracy, proper disclosures, and compliance with our editorial policy. Affiliate relationships are disclosed, claims are verified.</p>
					<span class="step-who">AI-assisted, policy-enforced</span>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="pipeline-step">
				<div class="step-number">5</div>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Publication &amp; distribution</h3>
					<p>Approved articles are published to the site, submitted to search engines, and distributed through our newsletter. Post-publication, we monitor performance and update content as tools and information change.</p>
					<span class="step-who">Automated</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2>The team</h2>
		<p>
			Superdots runs on <a href="https://paperclip.ing">Paperclip</a>, an AI agent orchestration platform.
			Our team consists of specialised AI agents — each with a defined role — coordinated and supervised by
			Luca Bartoccini, our founder and human editor.
		</p>
		<div class="team-grid">
			<div class="team-card">
				<div class="team-icon" aria-hidden="true">
					<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H8a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"/></svg>
				</div>
				<h3>Human oversight</h3>
				<p>Luca reviews strategic decisions, approves publication, manages the editorial calendar, and ensures every article meets our quality bar. No article goes live without human sign-off.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="team-card">
				<div class="team-icon" aria-hidden="true">
					<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 20h9"/><path d="M16.5 3.5a2.121 2.121 0 0 1 3 3L7 19l-4 1 1-4L16.5 3.5z"/></svg>
				</div>
				<h3>AI writers &amp; editors</h3>
				<p>Specialised agents handle research, drafting, SEO optimisation, and content formatting. Each agent follows strict guidelines and produces work that goes through review before publication.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="team-card">
				<div class="team-icon" aria-hidden="true">
					<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg>
				</div>
				<h3>Engineering &amp; infrastructure</h3>
				<p>AI agents also build and maintain the site itself — the code, deployment pipeline, SEO infrastructure, and newsletter system. All changes go through code review and automated testing.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2>What AI does well</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Research at scale.</strong> AI can analyse search trends, competitor content, and reader questions faster than any human team.</li>
			<li><strong>Consistent structure.</strong> Every article follows the same format: clear headings, actionable steps, FAQ sections. AI is good at maintaining this consistency across hundreds of articles.</li>
			<li><strong>Speed.</strong> We can cover more departments and use cases because AI handles the heavy lifting of first drafts.</li>
			<li><strong>Technical accuracy.</strong> For tool comparisons and feature lists, AI can systematically verify details across multiple sources.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Where humans add value</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Judgement calls.</strong> Is this advice actually useful? Would a real HR manager find this helpful? AI can draft, but humans decide what's worth publishing.</li>
			<li><strong>Quality control.</strong> AI can produce plausible-sounding nonsense. Human review catches the gaps between "sounds right" and "is right."</li>
			<li><strong>Editorial direction.</strong> Which topics matter? What's overhyped? When should we say "this tool isn't ready yet"? These decisions require experience and honest assessment.</li>
			<li><strong>Accountability.</strong> Someone real stands behind every article. If we get something wrong, there's a person who takes responsibility and fixes it.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Our commitment</h2>
		<p>We are transparent about using AI because we believe readers deserve to know how content is made. Here's what we commit to:</p>
		<div class="commitment-grid">
			<div class="commitment-card">
				<h3>Disclosure</h3>
				<p>Every page on this site includes an AI disclosure in the footer. This page exists so you know exactly what that means.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="commitment-card">
				<h3>Accuracy over speed</h3>
				<p>We'd rather publish fewer articles than publish inaccurate ones. If AI gets something wrong, we fix it and note the correction.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="commitment-card">
				<h3>No fake bylines</h3>
				<p>We don't pretend AI-assisted articles were written entirely by humans. Our author attribution reflects how content was actually created.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="commitment-card">
				<h3>Continuous improvement</h3>
				<p>We regularly review and update published articles. AI and the tools we cover change fast — our content should keep up.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<p>
			Have questions about our process? Read our <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>
			or reach out at <a href="mailto:privacy@superdots.sh">privacy@superdots.sh</a>.
		</p>
	</div>

	<NewsletterForm variant="banner" source="how-we-work" />
</Base>

<style>
	/* Prose */
	.prose {
		line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
	}
	.prose h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		margin-top: var(--space-10);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
	}
	.prose strong {
		color: var(--color-text-strong);
	}

	/* Pipeline steps */
	.pipeline {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--space-4);
		margin-top: var(--space-4);
	}
	.pipeline-step {
		display: flex;
		gap: var(--space-4);
		padding: var(--space-5);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
		background: var(--color-bg);
		transition: border-color var(--transition-fast);
	}
	.pipeline-step:hover {
		border-color: var(--color-primary);
	}
	.step-number {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 36px;
		height: 36px;
		border-radius: var(--radius-full);
		background: var(--sd-red-light);
		color: var(--color-primary);
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		flex-shrink: 0;
	}
	.step-content {
		flex: 1;
	}
	.step-content h3 {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-base);
		font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
		color: var(--color-text-strong);
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
	}
	.step-content p {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		line-height: var(--leading-normal);
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
	}
	.step-who {
		display: inline-block;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-xs);
		font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		color: var(--color-primary);
		background: var(--sd-red-light);
		padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-2);
		border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
	}

	/* Team grid */
	.team-grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-4);
		margin-top: var(--space-4);
	}
	.team-card {
		padding: var(--space-5);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
		background: var(--color-bg);
		transition: border-color var(--transition-fast);
	}
	.team-card:hover {
		border-color: var(--color-primary);
	}
	.team-icon {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 36px;
		height: 36px;
		border-radius: var(--radius-md);
		background: var(--sd-red-light);
		color: var(--color-primary);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
	}
	.team-card h3 {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-base);
		font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
		color: var(--color-text-strong);
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
	}
	.team-card p {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		line-height: var(--leading-normal);
		margin: 0;
	}

	/* Commitment grid */
	.commitment-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
		gap: var(--space-4);
		margin-top: var(--space-4);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
	}
	.commitment-card {
		padding: var(--space-5);
		border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		background: var(--color-bg);
	}
	.commitment-card h3 {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
		color: var(--color-primary);
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
	}
	.commitment-card p {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		line-height: var(--leading-normal);
		margin: 0;
	}

	@media (min-width: 640px) {
		.team-grid {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 480px) {
		.commitment-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
		.team-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
